Author, distribute and
update Minecraft packs

Usage: empack [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Author:
  init
          Create a project
          or import a
          modpack archive
  add
          Add a new
          dependency; use
          update to change
          an existing
          selection
  remove
          Remove projects
          from the modpack
  sync
          Reconcile
          installed content
          with recorded
          intent and exact
          selections
  update
          Preview dependency
          updates; use
          --apply to apply
          the reviewed
          changes
  pin
          Pin current
          provider
          selections; remove
          per-dependency
          automatic
          preferences
  unpin
          Remove provider
          pins while
          retaining the
          exact current
          selections
  adopt
          Accept verified
          installed changes
          without rewriting
          payloads
  migrate
          Plan or apply a
          runtime migration
          without editing
          live intent first
  manifest
          Inspect authoring
          intent and its
          exact lock without
          network access
  check
          Check current
          authoring,
          recorded
          relationships and
          applicable local
          content

Install:
  instance
          Manage exact
          releases in a
          separate installed
          game instance

Publish:
  build
          Build verified
          distribution
          archives
  release
          Sign and publish
          native releases
          for static HTTPS
          hosting

Tools:
  status
          Inspect workspace
          metadata without
          network access or
          durable changes
  doctor
          Inspect this
          binary and local
          tools; explicit
          Java/runtime
          options run a
          version probe
  pending
          Inspect, resume or
          discard saved
          build/import/sync/instance
          inputs
  recover
          Inspect or recover
          an interrupted
          engine operation
  clean
          Remove generated
          builds, caches or
          saved continuation
          data
  help
          Print this message
          or the help of the
          given
          subcommand(s)

Options:
  -w, --workdir <WORKDIR>
          Authoring project,
          publisher
          directory or
          installed instance
          root
          
          [env:
          EMPACK_WORKDIR=]

      --state-dir <STATE_DIR>
          Durable operation
          and recovery
          storage, separate
          from disposable
          caches
          
          [env:
          EMPACK_STATE_DIR=/Users/zer0cell/production/rules/terminal/evidence/20261123T225427626218Z-journeys/work/empack/state]

      --cache-dir <CACHE_DIR>
          Disposable cache
          root; previews
          only inspect
          existing objects
          
          [env:
          EMPACK_CACHE_DIR=/Users/zer0cell/production/rules/terminal/evidence/20261123T225427626218Z-journeys/work/empack/cache/empack]

  -j, --cpu-jobs <CPU_JOBS>
          Maximum concurrent
          engine workers
          
          [env:
          EMPACK_CPU_JOBS=]
          [default: 2]

  -n, --net-timeout <NET_TIMEOUT>
          Cumulative
          deadline in
          seconds for each
          catalog or payload
          acquisition phase
          
          [env:
          EMPACK_NET_TIMEOUT=]
          [default: 300]

      --curseforge-api-client-key <CURSEFORGE_API_CLIENT_KEY>
          CurseForge API
          Client Key
          
          [env:
          EMPACK_KEY_CURSEFORGE]

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Verbosity level
          (0=error, 1=warn,
          2=info, 3=debug,
          4=trace)
          
          [env:
          EMPACK_LOG_LEVEL=]
          [default: 0]

      --log-format <LOG_FORMAT>
          Log format:
          compact text, JSON
          events or pretty
          text
          
          [env:
          EMPACK_LOG_FORMAT=]
          [default: text]
          [possible values:
          text, json,
          pretty]

      --log-output <LOG_OUTPUT>
          Log output stream
          (stderr, stdout)

          Possible values:
          - stderr: STDERR
          - stdout: STDOUT
          
          [env:
          EMPACK_LOG_OUTPUT=]
          [default: stderr]

  -c, --color <COLOR>
          Color output
          control (auto,
          always, never)

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Let
            module detect
          - always:
            Explicitly
            enable (useful
            in
            non-interactive)
          - never:
            Explicitly
            disable (also
            useful in
            non-interactive)
          
          [env:
          EMPACK_COLOR=]
          [default: auto]

  -y, --yes
          Run without
          prompts;
          unresolved content
          choices still fail
          
          [env: EMPACK_YES=]

      --dry-run
          Preview changes
          without publishing
          project, instance
          or durable state
          
          [env:
          EMPACK_DRY_RUN=]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a
          summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Start a pack: empack init
my-pack
Author changes: empack
--workdir my-pack sync
Export for a launcher:
empack --workdir my-pack
build modrinth

Author commands use
empack.yml and empack.lock.
Instance commands manage a
separate installed game
directory.
Author update checks
dependency versions;
instance update checks
published pack releases.
Both preview by default; add
--apply to apply the
selected changes.
Neither command updates the
empack executable. Use
empack status to inspect a
workspace.
Use --dry-run before a
command to preview changes.
Run empack <command> --help
for its options.
